{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The voice of the lad.</b> From here — that the prayer of the sick person is more effective than the prayers of others on his behalf, and it takes precedence in being accepted (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Where he is.</b> According to the deeds that he does now he is judged, and not according to what he is destined to do (Rosh HaShanah 16) — for the ministering angels were pressing charges and saying: Master of the Universe, for one whose descendants are destined to kill Your children by thirst, You are raising up a well for him? And He answers them: Now what is he — righteous or wicked? They said to Him: Righteous. He said to them: According to his deeds now I judge him — and this is 'where he is.' And where did his descendants kill Israel by thirst? When Nebuchadnezzar exiled them, as it says: 'מַשָּׂא בַּעְרָב… לִקְרַאת צָמֵא הֵתָיוּ מַיִם…' (Isaiah 21). When they were leading them past the Arabs, Israel would say to their captors: Please, take us to the children of our kinsmen, Ishmael, and they will have pity on us — as it says 'אֹרְחוֹת דְּדָנִים' (ibid.) — do not read דְּדָנִים but דּוֹדִים. And they would come out to meet them and bring them salted meat and inflated waterskins, Israel thinking they were full of water; and when he puts it into his mouth and opens it, the air enters his body and he dies."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:49.915067927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}